## Peak-rating-based detection filtering

Retain lipid features detected by peak rating in at least 50% of samples in at least one group.

# =========================
# 5. Peak-rating-based detection filter
# =========================
DETECTION_THRESHOLD = 0.50

def pass_peak_rating_filter(row, threshold=DETECTION_THRESHOLD):
    for group, cols in PEAK_GROUPS.items():
        detection_rate = (row[cols] > 0).sum() / len(cols)
        if detection_rate >= threshold:
            return True
    return False

keep_mask = df.apply(pass_peak_rating_filter, axis=1)
df_filtered = df[keep_mask].copy()
filtered_full_file = TABLE_DIR / "Data_for_Python_peakRating50_filtered_full.csv"
df_filtered.to_csv(filtered_full_file, index=False)

print("Original features:", df.shape[0])
print("Features after peak-rating group-wise detection filter:", df_filtered.shape[0])
print("Saved:", filtered_full_file)

## Preprocessing

Peak-area values are median-normalized and log2-transformed. Pareto scaling is used for PCA and heatmap visualization only; volcano plots use log2-normalized values without Pareto scaling.

