## Notes for reporting

Suggested Methods wording:

> Lipid features were filtered using sample-level peak-rating information. Features were retained if they showed detectable peak ratings in at least 50% of samples in at least one experimental group. Quantitative analyses were performed using peak-area values of the retained features. Peak-area values were median-normalized and log2-transformed. Pareto scaling was applied for PCA and heatmap visualization. Pairwise differential lipid analysis was performed using Welch's t-test, and p-values were adjusted using the Benjamini-Hochberg false discovery rate method. Lipid-class-level analysis was performed by assigning features to lipid classes based on annotated compound names and summing peak areas within each class.
